{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1551149-good-resource-for-portraying-psychics-in-games","id":1551149,"title":"Good Resource for Portraying Psychics in Games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-20T00:16:16-07:00","id":1551149,"title":"Good Resource for Portraying Psychics in Games","content":"In the past, a Livejournal blog dating to the early 2010s that provided a critical analysis of psychic character in science fiction and fantasy, and I remember being struck by just how useful it could be in writing fiction about such individuals. It went into a serious degree of depth about the marginalization of psi powers, social ostracization of psychics, etc. While I don't agree with the author's political views, I do think that their observations could be quite useful when running some types of games. Glad that the author was able to write in-depth about such a specific minority.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the passage of time has eaten the blog's original URL, but I found a pretty good backup of it at the Wayback Machine. Without further ado, here you go.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20230122061556/https://critpsitheory.livejournal.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20230122061556im_/https://l-stat.livejournal.net/img/og_image.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20230122061556/https://critpsitheory.livejournal.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Working Toward a Critical Analytical Theory of Psi in SF/F </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20230122061556/https://critpsitheory.livejournal.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20230122061556